  "problem_statement": "Add `int scn_bool(const char *str, size_t n)` and `int scn_bool_str(const char *str)` to parse boolean strings. `scn_bool` must consider only the first `n` bytes of `str`, while `scn_bool_str` must consider the whole NUL-terminated string. Each function must return 1 when the considered string is exactly `1`, `true`, `yes`, or `on`; return 0 when it is exactly `0`, `false`, `no`, or `off`; and return -EINVAL otherwise. Matching must be case-sensitive. A NULL pointer or an empty string must return -EINVAL, and characters after the first `n` bytes must not affect the result.",
